WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.272
Spray the crust, and it does not harden all at once. The two

2
00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:06.926
binders set on different clocks, and that turns out to be useful.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.647
Gamma-P-G-A firms up within a few hours, giving early

4
00:00:11.747 --> 00:00:14.895
grip. The calcite ripens more slowly, across the full

5
00:00:14.995 --> 00:00:18.143
thirty-two-hour spray protocol, and ends up stronger.

6
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:22.907
So the fast polymer carries the crust through its fragile first

7
00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:25.959
day, while the calcite takes over as the long-term floor.

8
00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:29.683
Over months the polymer biodegrades first, then the calcite slowly

9
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:32.866
wears too. Because the calcite lasts longest, it is what

10
00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.650
sets how long you can wait before spraying again.

11
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:38.500
One caveat. The six-month cadence is where the field

12
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.644
trial stopped observing, not a measured service life. The

13
00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:44.070
crust was still stable when the trial ended.

